       en="Formal Greek uses **learned aorist passive participles** as nouns: *οι απελαθέντες* “those who were expelled”, *οι διωχθέντες* “the persecuted”, *οι πληγέντες* “those affected (by a disaster)”. They decline like ancient participles (*του απελαθέντος, των απελαθέντων*). Everyday Greek prefers a relative clause: *αυτοί που απελάθηκαν*. The perfect participle *εγκατεστημένος* “settled, established” is fully modern and common.",
